In acceptance/test_reconcile_payments.py, test_regression_issue_590 asserts:
  reconcile_payments([("b2", "120.00", "TRANSFER")], INVOICES) == {"b2": None}

But test_amount_matches (line 9) asserts the same input gives:
  reconcile_payments([("b2", "120.00", "TRANSFER")], INVOICES) == {"b2": "INV-000102"}

INVOICES has exactly one invoice with amount 12000 (INV-000102), so the correct behavior per spec rule 3 is to match it. test_regression_issue_590 has the wrong expected value and should expect {"b2": "INV-000102"}. This is blocking LEDGERLIB-120 from going green. Please fix or remove this test.

